## Issue / fix: fix(config): emit section and section_value in JSON output for config subcommands

## Description
## Problem

`claw config model --output-format json` returned the same envelope as `claw config --output-format json` — the section argument was parsed but discarded (`_section` parameter in `render_config_json`).

```json
// before: config model → identical to config (no section field)
{ "kind": "config", "merged_keys": 1, "loaded_files": 1, "files": [...] }

// after: config model
{ "kind": "config", "section": "model", "section_value": null,
  "merged_keys": 1, "loaded_files": 1, "files": [...] }
```

The text path (`render_config_report`) already handled section correctly; only the JSON path was broken.

## Fix

`render_config_json` now:
- Passes `section` through (was `_section`)
- Looks up the section value via `runtime_config.get()`, converting the internal `JsonValue` to `serde_json::Value` via `render()`+parse
- Emits `section` (string) and `section_value` (parsed JSON value or null)
- Returns `ok:false` + `error` for unsupported section tokens

## Test

`config_section_json_emits_section_and_value`: asserts no `section` field without section arg; `section`+`section_value` present for all known sections; `ok:false`+`error` for unknown section.

Pinpoint: ROADMAP #126

