## Issue / fix: Fix URL prefix matching to require path boundaries

## Description
## Summary

We're using `url.path().starts_with(self.root_url.path())` and similar logic in a few places, which treats `https://example.com/foobar` as a subpath of `https://example.com/foo`, when these should really be at path boundaries.

For S3/GCS endpoints, the configured endpoint URL now contributes both its realm and its path. Requests still match on the same realm or subdomains of that realm, as before, but they must also be under the endpoint URL's path using segment-aware prefix matching. For example, `https://example.com/private` matches `https://bucket.example.com/ private/...`, but not `https://bucket.example.com/public/...` or `https://example.com/private-bucket`.

