## Issue / fix: [Windows port PR8] feature: add Windows support

## Description
[PR8](https://github.com/zellij-org/zellij/issues/316#issuecomment-3920047803) of the Windows port.

This is the final PR of the Windows port effort.

Native Windows runtime for Zellij — ConPTY backend, named pipe IPC, console input handling, signal support, CI, and cross-platform test adaptations.

## Overview

This PR implements all Windows-specific runtime code needed to run Zellij natively on Windows. It builds on PRs 1–7 which refactored the codebase for cross-platform compilation. The key subsystems are:

- **ConPTY pseudo-terminal backend** — full lifecycle management
- **Named pipe IPC** with a dual-pipe protocol (replacing Unix domain sockets)
- **Dual-path console input** — native Console API vs raw VT byte parsing
- **Signal handling** — Ctrl+C/break/close and resize polling
- **Plugin/WASM fixes** — directory handles, path sanitization
- **CI** — Windows build and test jobs

## IPC: Named Pipes with Dual-Pipe Protocol

**Problem:** Unix domain sockets are bidirectional over a single fd. Windows named pipes are created in half-duplex mode. This simplifies implementation of overlapped IO.

**Solution:** Six abstraction functions in `zellij-utils/src/consts.rs` that wrap `interprocess::local_socket`:

| Function | Unix | Windows |
|----------|------|---------|
| `ipc_connect(path)` | `GenericFilePath` connect | `GenericNamespaced` connect |
| `ipc_bind(path)` | `GenericFilePath` listener | `GenericNamespaced` listener + PID marker file |
| 

